-- Concrete ask-when-uncertain witness (Dragan InterACT):
-- Before asking, both intents (true , false) are compatible (K w = (w ≡ w)), so P(w) = (w ≡ true) is
-- NOT safe to act on. After asking a binary query whose response r = true satisfies H w r w' := (w' ≡ r),
-- P becomes provably safe over WorldAfter K H true.
before-query-unsafe : Neg (SafeOver {Bool} (λ w → w ≡ w) (λ w → w ≡ true))
before-query-unsafe s = true≢false (sym (s false (λ i → false)))
